---
import GuideLayout from '../../components/GuideLayout.astro';

const title = 'How to Set Up 2FA on Kraken (TOTP Authenticator)';

const description =
  'Enable TOTP two-factor authentication on Kraken without a mobile app. Get the setup key from Kraken security settings and generate live, browser-based codes.';

---

<GuideLayout
  serviceName="Kraken"
  title={title}
  description={description}
  path="/guides/kraken/"
  dateModified="2026-11-23"
  datePublished="2026-11-09"
  lastReviewed="2026-11-23"
  sources={[
    {
      label: 'Kraken Support — How does two-factor authentication (2FA) for sign-in work?',
      href: 'https://support.kraken.com/articles/360000911823-how-does-two-factor-authentication-2fa-for-sign-in-work-',
      kind: 'official',
    },
    {
      label: 'Kraken Support — Using an authenticator app for 2FA',
      href: 'https://support.kraken.com/articles/360000572186-using-an-authenticator-app-for-two-factor-authentication-2fa-',
      kind: 'official',
    },
    {
      label: 'Kraken Support — Setting up the Global Settings Lock',
      href: 'https://support.kraken.com/articles/360000444963-setting-up-the-global-settings-lock-gsl-',
      kind: 'official',
    },
    {
      label: 'RFC 6238 — TOTP: Time-Based One-Time Password Algorithm',
      href: 'https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc6238',
      kind: 'independent',
    },
  ]}
  intro="Kraken has supported standard TOTP for years, and it stops account takeovers cold. Worth knowing: Kraken's highest-rated factor today is a passkey/security key, and the TOTP factor is scoped per “facet” (sign-in, trading, funding), so one enrollment is only the start."
  minutes={3}
  params={['6 digits', '30s period', 'SHA-1']}
  ctaTitle="Kraken's strength is the second secret you haven't enrolled yet"
  ctaBody="Sign-in 2FA protects the door; the Master key protects the vault — withdrawals, exports, and API permissions run on their own secret in Kraken. Finish both enrollments and keep them as two independent recent-key slots here."
  steps={[
    {
      title: 'Open Kraken security settings',
      body: 'Sign in at kraken.com and open Security settings. You’ll see “Sign-in Two-Factor Authentication (2FA)” — the facet that stops account takeovers on the login page itself. Kraken scopes 2FA per action: Trading, Funding and the Master key are set up separately. On the retail site the entry point is your profile icon → “Security & Access”; on pro.kraken.com it is profile icon → Settings → Security, where the per-function 2FA table lives.',
    },
    {
      title: 'Add the authenticator-app factor',
      body: 'Kraken recommends a passkey here — it is phishing-resistant, and Kraken says so explicitly. Prefer a portable TOTP code? Choose “Authenticator app” in the Sign-in 2FA section instead. Either way, Kraken’s Step-up 2FA then covers later changes: adding, editing or removing a 2FA method has to be confirmed with your passkey, an authenticator code or your Master Key before it goes through.',
    },
    {
      title: 'Reveal the secret',
      body: 'Kraken shows the QR together with the setup key — click “View setup key” to read it in plain text, and Kraken states plainly that storing that key is how you back the method up. Copy the key, or screenshot the QR and paste the image onto the generator page — it is decoded in your browser, never sent anywhere. Note the label: Kraken’s own troubleshooting warns to enter the code labelled “Kraken.com Sign-in”, not “Kraken.com Master Key”, once you run both.',
    },
    {
      title: 'Generate, verify, activate',
      body: 'Paste into 2facounter.com, copy the live code, and paste it back into Kraken’s confirmation field. Kraken then flips that function’s OFF/ON dial to on and shows “2FA app” as the method — codes are now required per that function.',
    },
    {
      title: 'Harden the rest',
      body: 'Add Kraken’s Master Key, enable withdrawal address whitelisting, and keep the separate secrets for sign-in and Master key in your password manager — Kraken’s guidance is explicit that the two should live on different devices, and never in the same authenticator app. If you ever lose both, Kraken’s route back is the Account Recovery Photo process, which is worth reading before you need it.',
    },
  ]}
  faqs={[
    {
      q: 'Do I need the Kraken mobile app for 2FA?',
      a: 'No. Kraken’s TOTP factor is standard RFC 6238 — any authenticator works, including a purely browser-based one. The mobile app is one carrier, not a requirement.',
    },
    {
      q: 'What are Kraken’s “facets” for 2FA?',
      a: 'Kraken lets you require separate factors for logging in, for trading, for funding (withdrawals), and for account-level changes (Master key). Stronger setups have sign-in on TOTP and the Master key on a different secret — you can maintain both recent-key slots in this generator.',
    },
    {
      q: 'What is the Global Settings Lock?',
      a: 'Kraken’s GSL freezes changes to your account and hides sensitive information — the last line of defence if your password and sign-in 2FA are both compromised. Its own guidance: once the GSL is on you cannot add or change 2FA or your Master Key, so set both up first, and set the Master Key up before the GSL specifically. A Master Key enrolled beforehand can release the lock immediately; without one you sit out the full unlock period, and Kraken Support cannot shorten it.',
    },
    {
      q: 'Codes rejected right after setup — what broke?',
      a: 'Most often it is clock drift — Kraken, like every exchange, validates against strict time windows, and an unsynced clock drifts outside them quickly. Enable automatic time sync in your operating system and retry with the next code before assuming anything worse.',
    },
  ]}
/>
